module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.TransferInstance
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Isomorphisms
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.IsTensorProduct
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Maps
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.FibreProduct
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.MilnorPatching.AdjunctionUnit
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Localization.Glueing.CategoricalPullback

/-!
# Modules over a base change of a ring fibre product

Start from a cartesian square `B' = B ×_A A'` in which `A' → A` is surjective, and add a ring map
`B' → D'`.  Base change along it produces the three rings `D = D' ⊗_{B'} B`, `C' = D' ⊗_{B'} A'`
and `C = D' ⊗_{B'} A`, and the square of `D'`, `D`, `C'`, `C` is again a square of the same shape.
A `D'`-module therefore extends to a compatible pair of a `D`-module and a `C'`-module, and this
relative comparison functor again has a right adjoint with invertible counit: a compatible pair
glues to the `D'`-module `N ×_{M'/IM'} M'`.

This is the setting in which the finiteness and flatness statements of Section 15.7 of the source
are proved; the absolute square of Section 15.6 is the case `D' = B'`.

## Main definitions

* `MilnorPatching.RelativeModuleFibreProductSituation` is Stacks Tag 08KK: the extra ring map
  `B' → D'`, together with the three base-change rings `D`, `C'`, `C`, the structural maps out of
  `B'`, the canonical surjection `D' → D ×_C C'`, and the literal quotient `M'/IM'`.
* `MilnorPatching.extensionOfScalarsToTensorProductPullback` is Stacks Tag 08KL: the relative
  comparison functor from `D'`-modules to compatible pairs.
* `MilnorPatching.RelativeCompatiblePairs` is the glued module `N ×_{M'/IM'} M'`.

## Main results

* `MilnorPatching.image_extendedKernel_eq_extendedIdeal` is Stacks Tag 08KN: the ideal `J D'`
  generated by the kernel `J` of `B' → B` surjects onto the ideal `I C'`.
* `MilnorPatching.relativeCompatiblePairsRightAdjoint_counit_isIso` is Stacks Tag 08KM: the
  relative comparison functor has a right adjoint whose values are the relative compatible pairs
  and whose counit is an isomorphism, so extending a glued module back to `D` and `C'` recovers
  the two components canonically and naturally.

## Implementation notes

Mathlib puts the scalar ring first in an extension-of-scalars tensor product, so the displayed
tensor factors are reversed from the source throughout.  The rings carry independent universes;
the module categories share one upper universe together with an independent module universe
parameter, and the algebra structures needed to form the tensor products are installed locally to
keep global instance resolution unambiguous.  Tag 08KK is a situation rather than a lemma, so its
content is the structure together with the constructions attached to it; the surjectivity of
`D' → D ×_C C'`, the commuting functor square and the `D`-linear comparison with the literal
quotient are proved here, each characterized by its formula on pure tensors.  The gluing condition
for the right adjoint is stated over `C` and then rewritten over `M'/IM'` by that comparison.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KN)
-/

section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open ModuleGlueing

universe uB' uB uA' uA uD' v

namespace MilnorPatching
open ModuleGlueing
@[expose] public section

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 08KL.** After base change along a `B'`-algebra `D'`, extension
of scalars gives the functor
`Mod D' \longrightarrow Mod (D' \otimes_{B'} B) \times_{Mod (D' \otimes_{B'} A)}
Mod (D' \otimes_{B'} A')`.

It sends a module `L'` to its scalar extensions to `D' \otimes_{B'} B` and
`D' \otimes_{B'} A'`, equipped with the canonical identification after extending both
once more to `D' \otimes_{B'} A`. -/
@[stacks 08KL]
noncomputable def extensionOfScalarsToTensorProductPullback
    {B' : Type uB'} {B : Type uB} {A' : Type uA'} {A : Type uA} {D' : Type uD'}
    [CommRing B'] [CommRing B] [CommRing A'] [CommRing A]
    [CommRing D'] [Algebra B' B] [Algebra B' A'] [Algebra B' A] [Algebra B' D']
    (BtoA : B →ₐ[B'] A) (A'toA : A' →ₐ[B'] A) :
    ModuleCat.{max v uD' uB uA' uA} D' ⥤
      CategoricalPullback
        (ModuleCat.extendScalars.{_, _, max v uD' uB uA' uA}
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B' D') BtoA).toRingHom)
        (ModuleCat.extendScalars.{_, _, max v uD' uB uA' uA}
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B' D') A'toA).toRingHom) :=
  extensionOfScalarsToPullback
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom (R := B') (A := D') (B := B))
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom (R := B') (A := D') (B := A'))
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B' D') BtoA).toRingHom
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B' D') A'toA).toRingHom
    (by ext x; simp)

end

end MilnorPatching

end

